      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f4842afc-ff4c-528e-b030-2123c0367083",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jonny Greenwood, Stanley Donwood, John Leckie, Nigel Godrich\n- Bands: Radiohead\n- Albums: Jonny Greenwood Is the Controller, The Bends\n- Record Labels: Trojan Records, Parlophone Records, Capitol Records\n\nFacts:\n- On 13 March 1995, Radiohead released its second studio album, The Bends, through Parlophone Records in the United Kingdom and Capitol Records in the United States.\n- John Leckie produced The Bends, and Nigel Godrich engineered it.\n- Nigel Godrich later went on to co-produce all future Radiohead albums.\n- Since The Bends in 1995, Stanley Donwood has provided the artwork for every Radiohead album.\n- Jonny Greenwood of Radiohead created the compilation album Jonny Greenwood Is the Controller, and Trojan Records released it.\n- Jonny Greenwood Is the Controller features artwork by Stanley Donwood.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f5564829-4d32-59a2-977c-20cbbeef0497",
        "text": "Page: Jonny Greenwood Is the Controller. Sentence: Jonny Greenwood Is the Controller is a compilation album created by Jonny Greenwood of Radiohead and released on Trojan Records.\nPage: Jonny Greenwood Is the Controller. Sentence: The album features artwork by Stanley Donwood, who has provided art for every Radiohead album since \"The Bends\" (1995).\nPage: The Bends. Sentence: The Bends (stylised as the bends) is the second studio album by the English alternative rock band Radiohead, released on 13 March 1995 by Parlophone Records in the United Kingdom and by Capitol Records in the United States.\nPage: The Bends. Sentence: The album was produced by John Leckie and engineered by Nigel Godrich, who would go on to co-produce all future albums by the band.",
